# Godot 4+ specific ignores
.godot/
/android/

# Godot-specific ignores
.import/
export.cfg
export_presets.cfg

# Imported translations (automatically generated from CSV files)
*.translation

# Mono/C#-specific ignores
.mono/
data_*/
mono_crash.*.json

# OpenLot run/test capture output (regenerated by every headless test run:
# NetSelfTest / GizmoSelfTest / NetIntegrationTest). These are logs, not sources.
*.log

# Editor and OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# NOTE: *.uid, *.import and *.godot files ARE intentionally tracked.
# Godot treats *.uid as the stable resource identity for a script/asset and
# regenerating it on another machine can silently break res:// references,
# so they belong in version control.
#
# NOTE: addons/dear-imgui-godot/target/ IS intentionally tracked.
# Those are the prebuilt Dear ImGui GDExtension binaries the project actually
# loads at runtime (see addons/dear-imgui-godot/dear-imgui-godot.gdextension).
# Upstream ships them as a distribution artifact and this repo carries no Rust
# crate source to rebuild them from, so ignoring them would leave a fresh clone
# unable to start. Revisit only if the addon is vendored as a submodule or the
# Rust crate is added back to the repo.
